    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp35Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") detection for `POST /api/owners`. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, but flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with getters/setters and `@Column` mappings.\n\n2. **New OfficeFloor step** `CheckPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 runs after `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (so a hard duplicate is already ruled out) and before `SaveOwner`. It scans existing owners for one with the same last name (case-insensitive) and same non-blank postcode but a different telephone, and mutates the built owner: `possibleDuplicate = true` / `possibleDuplicateOf = <lowest matching id>`, else `false`/absent.\n\n3. **Pipeline wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `checkPossibleDuplicate` step between `checkIdentity` and `save`, governed by the same transaction.\n\n4. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added the two `readOnly` properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them (MapStruct maps them by name automatically), making them visible on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n5. **DB schema + seed data** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four DB `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended the two matching `NULL` values to each `owners` seed insert in the corresponding `data.sql` files.",
